+# Design
+
+The implementation will treat the order's persisted customer id and customer-facing snapshot fields as the historical source of truth. Order retrieval queries must therefore avoid inner joins to the live customer for admin detail and list operations; a nullable association or no association is acceptable, but the scalar customer id must remain queryable.
+
+The order repository/service query will use a real Spring `Pageable` with zero-based page numbers, a stable descending order timestamp/id, and predicates for status, email, customer name, and order id. The resulting `Page` will supply both the page content and complete count. Customer-specific lookup will use the same customer-id predicate and will not call `CustomerService` as a prerequisite. Read population will conditionally omit the customer while preserving order snapshot fields.
+
+Customer deletion and registration will be checked so foreign-key behavior does not cascade-delete orders or reuse an old customer identity. Add focused tests at the service/repository level and API integration coverage for deleted-account retrieval, empty customer ids, later pages, totals, and same-email re-registration.
