+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Deleting a customer currently makes historical orders inaccessible because the admin APIs require the live customer entity, and the paged order query loses its filters/page state. Support needs durable order records and reliable browsing after account closure.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Keep order snapshots (customer id, placed email, billing, and delivery data) usable after the referenced customer is deleted.
+- Make the customer-order endpoint query by stored customer id and return zero results rather than 404 when the account is gone or has no orders.
+- Correct admin order pagination, totals, newest-first ordering, and filtered page navigation.
+- Ensure a later registration using the deleted email creates an independent account with no access to the deleted account's orders.
+- Add regression coverage for deleted customers, filtering, pagination, and account recreation.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `order-history`: Durable historical order retrieval and administration independent of a live customer account.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+The order API, order facade/service/repository query path, customer deletion relationship handling, order read populators, and integration/service tests are affected. Existing order detail, status, history, and transaction behavior must remain available.
